{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 33","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_33&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Use the graph to determine the interval(s) on which the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is constant.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_33&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6b782f7f47cd33b60d59268a7f99bdef215284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\  (-\\infty,-4)\\cup(4,\\infty) \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\  (-\\infty,-3)\\cup(1,\\infty) \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\  (-4,4) \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\  (-3,-1) \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\  (-5,-3)\\cup(1,5) \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"886\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_33&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The parts of a function that are constant are where the value of the function doesn't change. At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d924f912a4072521e9bb4c86d868591e01d0f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />, the function stops being constant. At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, the function starts becoming constant again. This best matches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065158e41899bdf66823d0766340fe10d1f85b64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } (-\\infty,-3)\\cup(1,\\infty)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"195\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>¬anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest\">2025 TMTA Algebra I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_32\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 32\">Problem 32</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_34\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 34\">Problem 34</a></b>\n</td></tr